      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "These distance maidens can be a little tricky but we get a good line on most of these with five of the eight coming through the 1900m maiden at Mildura on Aug 8. SPICY APPLE (4) was the first home of the five, just failing to run down $1.45fav Glouf after finishing powerfully, and he deserves to be considered the testing material. WHERE EAGLES DARE (5) finished fourth in that Mildura race, but he was probably the best run of the beaten brigade outside SPICY APPLE after being forced wide rounding the bend. He'll relish the extra trip. To the contrary, AFFINEDEEL (1) saved ground rounding the bend at Mildura to just edge out WHERE EAGLES DARE for third but that was only the second run back from a spell so he should more improvement to come than others out of that race. JULEP (8) is the one that brings a different formline and now looks ready for this trip. BOUCHEREIGN (2) should be ready to peak fourth-up from a good gate and gets blinkers.",
